    <h2>Aside &amp; apparatus (§10.6–§10.9) — added Phase 5.11</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="font-size: 13.5px;">
      Same job as 3.9/4.11: the components 5.6–5.8 built get a home outside a full article
      render. The aside renders both its forms — the &gt;=1280 column
      (share/reply/progress-with-text) and the &lt;1280 relocated bar (<code
        >ReadingProgress bare</code
      >, what <code>Masthead.astro</code> mounts under itself) — side by side rather than one
      disappearing into the other at a real viewport width. Author block, prev/next and the
      related grid below are real
      <code>writing</code> entries (article 003 and its neighbours), not invented data.
    </p>
    <div class="aside-demo-row">
      <div class="aside-demo">
        <p class="aside-demo-label">&gt;=1280 — the aside column</p>
        <ArticleAside title={current.title} />
      </div>
      <div class="aside-demo aside-demo--bare">
        <p class="aside-demo-label">&lt;1280 — relocated under the masthead</p>
        <ReadingProgress bare />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="measure-demo">
      <ArticleApparatus
        headings={apparatusHeadings}
        numberedHeadingFlags={apparatusFlags}
        prev={apparatusPrev}
        next={apparatusNext}
        related={apparatusRelated}
      />
    </div>

    <h2>Tag (component 08, §6·08) — added Phase 6.3</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="font-size: 13.5px;">
      Three variants as props, not three components (§22.6). Plain and counted are both
      real links to <code>/writing/tag/&lt;tag&gt;</code>; tab to either and the token
      focus ring should show. Current has no <code>href</code> at all — not tabbable, by construction
      rather than a disabled/aria-current workaround.
    </p>
    <div class="tag-row">
      <Tag tag="ansible" variant="plain" />
      <Tag tag="infrastructure" variant="counted" count={11} />
      <Tag tag="all" variant="current" count={38} />
      <Tag tag="ctf" variant="current" />
      <Tag tag="homelab" variant="plain" />
    </div>

